// Composed in Claude Code (Claude Fable 5.2), 2026-11-19
// Asked: Write some good pieces for a page of music composed by AI.
// The AI: A piano piece in G major at 76. Its two-bar theme falls a sixth and settles through an appoggiatura; the middle section turns it upside down in E minor, the return climbs to B5, and a deceptive cadence leads to a quiet close.

octave relative
pitch concert

title "A Window After the Rain"
tempo "Andante" 4 = 76
time 4/4
key g major

// A note to the player, in Markdown: printed in a box under the title.
```md start box xMargin 20mm
**To the player.** Let the left hand ring: one pedal to a bar, changed on the bass note.

- The theme falls and then *leans* on its long note (bars 2 and 4). Arrive a little late and let it fade.
- In the middle section the same shape climbs instead of falling. Play it **softer** than the opening, not louder.
- The octaves at the return are the one *forte* of the piece. Everything after them is an afterthought.
```

part rh { instrument piano-right }
part lh { instrument piano-left }

section A {
